		(uuid "12b39720-71eb-43c1-937b-417dfe1faa18")
	)
	(text "DESIGN NOTES\n1. Battery-backed architecture: USB-C 5 V charges the 1S Li-ion through U3; the system always runs from VBAT via U4.\n2. Charge current = 1000 V / R3 = 455 mA (0.15C for a 3000 mAh cell; stays inside the USB 2.0 500 mA budget).\n3. U4 is a 25 uA-Iq 3.0 V LDO. 3.0 V keeps the ESP32-C3 in spec down to ~3.25 V cell voltage.\n4. Load-cell excitation is regulated by Q1 and switched off when HX711 PD_SCK is held high (power-down).\n   EXC+ = 1.25 V x (1 + R12/R13) = 2.75 V. RATE = 0 (10 SPS), internal oscillator.\n5. VBAT_ADC = VBAT x 330k / 1.33M (4.2 V -> 1.04 V, ADC atten 2.5 dB). Divider draws 3.2 uA.\n6. IO9 uses the module internal pull-up; pull it low on J4 while toggling EN for UART download.\n7. Sleep budget: ESP32-C3 deep sleep ~5 uA + LDO 25 uA + divider 3 uA + HX711 PD <1 uA."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 30.48 228.6 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "c36ce7df-7a75-41e8-b1a3-b787e13e09d7")
	)
